1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,805
<i>Don't you think it's about time</i>
<i>you reinstated me?</i>

3
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:15,515
<i>I will not reinstate you.</i>

4
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:20,812
<i>Arnaldo will run for governor</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente</i>

5
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:22,313
<i>in the next election.</i>

6
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:24,190
[Jepoy] <i>You got everything</i>
<i>you wanted from me.</i>

7
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:26,359
<i>I'm of no more use now. Let me go!</i>

8
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:30,155
[Julio] <i>Bring me Alvarez's head,</i>
<i>and I'll set you free.</i>

9
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:32,157
<i>There's going to be a new king.</i>

10
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:35,869
<i>And I'm pretty sure</i>
<i>he will have his own queen.</i>

11
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>I will not be pushed</i>
<i>to the sidelines, Auntie.</i>

12
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:41,166
<i>Especially once I prove to my family</i>

13
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:45,545
<i>that Ivy Aguas is connected</i>
<i>to Camia Cruz and Madrigal.</i>

14
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:49,007
<i>And when that happens,</i>
<i>I'll be the hero of the family.</i>

15
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,049
[Diego] <i>They're all cunning.</i>

16
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:53,052
<i>They might let Jepoy live</i>
<i>as long as he's useful to them.</i>

17
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,096
<i>-And if he isn't?</i>
<i>-They'll kill him.</i>

18
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,097
<i>I need to save Jepoy.</i>

19
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:57,140
<i>-Get out of my way.</i>
<i>-No.</i>

20
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:59,976
<i>-What's wrong with you?</i>
<i>-Yes, he's your friend! But I love you!</i>

21
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,021
<i>Ivy, trust me. I'll get Jepoy back.</i>

22
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,773
<i>I'll bring him back safe and sound.</i>

23
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:06,441
[goon] <i>Madrigal escaped.</i>

24
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>Damn it!</i>

25
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:09,444
[Jepoy] <i>I'm the time bomb</i>
<i>they're waiting on to explode</i>

26
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:10,904
<i>so they'll find out who you really are.</i>

27
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:11,946
<i>The danger of them finding out</i>

28
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:13,531
<i>about your real plans will still be there.</i>

29
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,658
<i>I have to cut ties with you.</i>

30
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:17,535
[Ivy] <i>I can't believe it.</i>

31
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:20,538
<i>How did Madrigal manage to escape?</i>

32
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:23,833
<i>Maybe because he had</i>
<i>an accomplice within our circle?</i>

33
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:25,960
<i>Don't be stupid.</i>

34
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,378
<i>Or have you forgotten</i>

35
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:30,507
<i>Miss Aguas' transgressions</i>
<i>against our family?</i>

36
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:33,510
<i>If you focus on this</i>
<i>unfounded suspicion against Ivy,</i>

37
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:34,511
<i>we're going to have a problem.</i>

38
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:39,516
[Emilia] <i>I won't allow my son</i>
<i>to be used by someone</i>

39
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,810
<i>who could betray our family.</i>

40
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:45,230
<i>That's why I helped you</i>
<i>find Governor Alvarez.</i>

41
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:48,650
<i>To prove my loyalty to your family.</i>

42
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:52,070
<i>As for me and Arnaldo, we aren't official.</i>

43
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:54,864
<i>But once that happens, I'll text you.</i>

44
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,579
When Emilia got sick,

45
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:05,792
William Alvarez was
the first person I thought of

46
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:09,462
who could replace her as governor.

47
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:13,341
He was the perfect choice
for governor on paper.

48
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:16,803
He was well-educated,
and he came from a good family.

49
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:22,809
That's why it hurts to admit
and to tell everyone

50
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:26,104
the truth that the person
I chose to become governor

51
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,731
hid behind a mask.

52
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:32,902
And behind that mask
was the face of a traitor.

53
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:38,408
A traitor who found his way
into public office.

54
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,661
The rumors that
you've been hearing are true.

55
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:49,961
It's true that Governor Alvarez
stole public funds,

56
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:53,089
which were supposed to be
used for government projects.

57
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:57,468
Now that he's gone,
may his death be a warning

58
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:02,515
to all those who are planning
to betray the public's trust.

59
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:06,394
And, it's only fitting
that the one who'll replace him

60
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:10,231
is someone who's honest, fearless,

61
00:03:10,315 --> 00:03:13,359
and willing to offer their life

62
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:17,196
for the future of the residents
of Poblacion Ardiente.

63
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,407
Allow me to introduce to you…

64
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,911
the person who will be
running for governor

65
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:24,454
in the next election.

66
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:27,582
He's none other than my grandson,

67
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:29,334
and the current mayor of this town,

68
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:33,796
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo!

69
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,882
[applause]

70
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:44,641
[Arnaldo] Thank you.

71
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,394
[farmer 1] We will fight for Diego!

72
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,687
Fight!

73
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:52,440
[Dolfo] We will fight for the
farmers of Poblacion Ardiente!

74
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:53,691
Fight!

75
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:54,817
[farmer 2] Long live Diego!

76
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:58,363
Go, Diego! Diego! Diego!

77
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:04,202
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

78
00:04:04,661 --> 00:04:07,455
[Arnaldo] My fellowmen,
as your long-term mayor,

79
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:11,542
I'm asking all of you to
support and join our family

80
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:16,381
in condemning a corrupt traitor,
William Alvarez.

81
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:21,844
Along with hunting down
another traitor named Madrigal

82
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:25,682
and the man who helped him evade justice.

83
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:29,143
Let's put an end to the silence
they've imposed upon us,

84
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:30,812
especially when we try to speak

85
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:33,314
against the current government's actions.

86
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:36,901
Let's put an end to
the suffering of our fellowmen

87
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:40,947
under the vicious and unfair
governance of the Ardientes!

88
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:44,742
Our town won't prosper if we don't get rid

89
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,246
of the weeds that pollute where we live.

90
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:50,373
[Diego] Let's show the Ardientes

91
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:54,127
that we're sick and tired
of a political dynasty!

92
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:56,504
We're sick and tired of crimes

93
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:59,048
and the oppression of human rights!

94
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:02,385
Now's the time to establish
a new government.

95
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,262
A government that will truly understand

96
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,889
the problems of its people.

97
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,310
It's time for a new Ardiente!

98
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:13,021
As your next governor,

99
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:17,025
I promise you that we will take this town

100
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:20,862
to even greater heights.

101
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:22,989
[applause]

102
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:31,414
-[farmer] Long live Diego!
-[all] Long live Diego!

103
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:34,792
Diego! Diego! Diego!

104
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:41,758
Diego! Diego! Diego!
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

105
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:47,263
Ivy, can we talk?

106
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:50,475
Why? Do you have another issue?

107
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:53,519
Are you going to call me a leech,

108
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:56,564
traitor, and manipulator again?

109
00:05:56,647 --> 00:06:00,443
You know, Ivy, those aren't
the only names I can call you.

110
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:01,652
There are many more.

111
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:05,156
But that can change, just as
long as you cooperate with me.

112
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:08,701
[sighs] Get to the point,
Emilia. Cut to the chase.

113
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:13,998
Okay. I want you to support
my bid for governor.

114
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,958
I need financial backing.

115
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:18,961
[chuckles]

116
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:24,467
Emilia, you're making it
a habit to beg money from me.

117
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:27,595
Why would I lend you money?

118
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:31,474
You know my loyalty lies
with your son, Arnaldo.

119
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:33,726
Oh, really?

120
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:38,231
What you're saying contradicts
what these pictures show.

121
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:42,527
Let me see.

122
00:06:56,499 --> 00:07:00,378
These? What are you implying?

123
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:03,256
That I'm Madrigal's accomplice?

124
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:06,801
Then, why are you so interested

125
00:07:06,884 --> 00:07:08,970
in what could happen to Madrigal?

126
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:13,307
You even gave us information
so we could pin down Alvarez.

127
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:20,064
Emilia, you're making me laugh.
You're hilarious.

128
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:25,069
Just because you can't get what you want

129
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,280
doesn't mean you need
to resort to blackmail.

130
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:28,656
You're pathetic.

131
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:31,242
And you are a lying witch.

132
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:38,207
Emilia. Those pictures are
taken from public events.

133
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:42,962
They can't prove that
I'm on Madrigal's side,

134
00:07:43,045 --> 00:07:44,547
or that I'm his accomplice.

135
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:48,968
So, if I were you, fire your investigator

136
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:51,053
because you're making a fool of yourself.

137
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:55,892
I know, Emilia, things are not
going well for you.

138
00:07:55,975 --> 00:08:00,813
But please, please, Emilia.
Stop humiliating yourself.

139
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:01,898
Please.

140
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:21,209
Mom, I heard that you fought
with Ivy again.

141
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:23,127
I found something.

142
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,756
Madrigal and Ivy Aguas
are working together.

143
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,136
Oh, come on. This doesn't prove anything!

144
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,013
If that were true,

145
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:36,307
Ivy would've rescued
Madrigal a long time ago!

146
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,686
Arnaldo, what did that woman
feed you for you

147
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:41,938
to think that way?

148
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:43,231
Don't you see?

149
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:44,815
Can't you see that Ivy is working

150
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,943
with the people betraying us?

151
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:50,029
And the only reason why we're keeping her

152
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,656
is because of her money!

153
00:08:53,282 --> 00:08:54,575
That's it. Enough.

154
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:58,621
Arnaldo, I just don't
want you to get hurt.

155
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:02,375
But you will when you find out
that Ivy is using you.

156
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:05,545
I said enough.

157
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:07,672
Okay?

158
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:10,174
You're just upset because
you didn't become governor,

159
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:12,385
and Ivy didn't back you up!

160
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:14,220
And, now?!

161
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:19,642
You just want everyone
to be miserable just like you!

162
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:22,520
And how dare you talk to me
that way, Arnaldo?!

163
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:26,649
How dare you?

164
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,241
This is for you.

165
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:37,994
It's not too much, but I hope it can help.

166
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:39,829
[man 1] Thank you, Mayor.

167
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:40,997
-[man 2] Thank you, Mayor.
-[Arnaldo] Okay.

168
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,206
[Arnaldo] Take care.

169
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:49,255
I see that you even give money
to the volunteers.

170
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:53,676
Of course, Miss Aguas.
Money makes the world go round.

171
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,554
Oh, and speaking of money.

172
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:01,434
I presume you'll also help us financially

173
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:04,520
with Arnaldo's campaign?

174
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,856
I remember you promised me
something like that.

175
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:08,065
[chuckles]

176
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:10,526
Of course, Congressman.

177
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:12,778
I have faith in Arnaldo.

178
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:15,323
That's why I'll provide him
one hundred percent

179
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:18,451
financial support
in his political campaign.

180
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,454
One hundred percent?

181
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:27,293
So, does that mean you won't
support any other candidate?

182
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,837
Just Arnaldo?

183
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,673
You can count on me, Congressman.

184
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:40,806
Thank you.

185
00:10:50,107 --> 00:10:51,108
[Camia] What about the noodles?

186
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,568
[farmer 1] We still have plenty
of it, ma'am.

187
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,654
[Camia] All right, you should
eat too, okay?

188
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:56,947
[Camia] Right. How's it going?

189
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,115
-[farmer 2] It's good, ma'am.
-[Camia] Good.

190
00:10:58,199 --> 00:10:59,950
[farmer 2] I'm about to finish this.

191
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:04,789
Diego! Nimfa said that her workmates

192
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:09,502
from San Bartolome
would come and help us too.

193
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:11,003
-Great!
-They're glad to know

194
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,046
you're running.

195
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:13,631
They'll support you with your campaign.

196
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:15,341
They're willing to volunteer.

197
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:16,842
-Nice.
-Wow.

198
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:19,345
-Thank you, Nanny.
-I'll tell them that.

199
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:21,764
Everyone!

200
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:25,851
Thank you for all your support.

201
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:30,147
I must admit,
I still don't know how to start,

202
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,273
and I don't have the means

203
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:32,942
compared to what the Ardientes do.

204
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:35,528
But every time I see how united we are,

205
00:11:36,195 --> 00:11:37,947
I get the courage to fight.

206
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:40,032
You can count on us, Diego!

207
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,785
We've always wanted you to run,

208
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:44,745
but we understand that you didn't want

209
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,038
to go up against your family.

210
00:11:46,122 --> 00:11:49,250
-But you finally woke up.
-Right.

211
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,793
[laughs]

212
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:55,172
Like all of you, and the people
of Ardiente,

213
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:57,258
I finally decided to do the right thing.

214
00:11:57,341 --> 00:11:58,884
-[Pandoy] Correct.
-[farmer 3] Right.

215
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:01,011
[suspenseful music playing]

216
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:10,646
[phone ringing]

217
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:11,730
[Fernan] Look, it's almost--

218
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:13,232
-I'll just take this.
-[Fernan] That's good.

219
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:15,526
-[Loring] Okay.
-[phone ringing]

220
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:17,570
Hello, Ivy?

221
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,866
Diego. The Ardientes have
started mobilizing their units.

222
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,326
<i>They're also looking for Jepoy.</i>

223
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:26,078
Tomorrow, they'll go to the cooperative.

224
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,329
So, be ready.

225
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:29,665
I just want to tell you

226
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:34,211
that I may be far away from you,
but you have my full support.

227
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:36,755
I know, Ivy.

228
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:38,591
<i>We'll be ready.</i>

229
00:12:38,674 --> 00:12:40,468
There's no turning back, Ivy.

230
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,183
-You should eat first.
-It's good.

231
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:48,392
[Camia] Take a break.

232
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:49,477
Everyone!

233
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,145
I've got news.

234
00:12:51,812 --> 00:12:53,439
I received a lead saying

235
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:56,192
the Ardientes will come here tomorrow.

236
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:57,067
What? But why?

237
00:12:57,151 --> 00:13:00,946
I know we have yet to come up
with concrete plans…

238
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:04,950
But we're talking to possible
sponsors and supporters

239
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,118
who could help with Diego's campaign.

240
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:11,957
Diego, why don't you seek help
from Miss Ivy?

241
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:14,001
-That's right! Yes!
-Isn't that right, friends?

242
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:19,381
I mean, she helped us when
the Ardientes took our land before.

243
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:22,343
So, I'm sure Miss Ivy
will also help Diego.

244
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:24,845
-[Fernan] Right.
-[Pandoy] She'll help you, son.

245
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:27,806
Even if she doesn't help financially, her
moral support will be more than enough.

246
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:30,559
You two are good friends, right?

247
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:31,894
[Pandoy] That's right.

248
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:33,896
I'm sorry…

249
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:37,733
but Miss Aguas decided
to support the Ardientes.

250
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:42,488
So, it's better for us to do
this without her help this time.

251
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:45,824
Everyone, let's just eat for now.

252
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,576
-[farmer 4] Come on.
-[Fernan] Talk to him.

253
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,577
-[Pandoy] But…
-[Fernan] Talk to him.

254
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:50,329
-All right, Miss Camia.
-[Pandoy] How come? How?

255
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:56,627
You know what to do.

256
00:13:56,710 --> 00:14:00,381
If you need to search every nook
and cranny in this town, do it.

257
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:03,467
Until you find Madrigal. Understood?

258
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:05,970
-Yes, Mayor.
-You can go now.

259
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:19,900
[Jepoy] <i>Ivy, I'm the key.</i>

260
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,444
<i>I'm the time bomb</i>
<i>they're waiting on to explode</i>

261
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,446
<i>so they'll find out who you really are.</i>

262
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:28,325
<i>I have to cut ties with you.</i>

263
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:34,248
<i>I have to stay away from you, Ivy.</i>

264
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:40,880
<i>I'll leave. But once I come back…</i>

265
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:46,343
<i>I'll have what I need to bring</i>
<i>the Ardientes to their knees.</i>

266
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:07,573
Congressman, we checked every
house in Poblacion Ardiente.

267
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:09,074
No sign of Madrigal.

268
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:12,202
He probably left town.

269
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,330
Okay, Mario. You may go.

270
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:23,547
Our enemies should never escape
the claws of the Ardientes.

271
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:29,345
Grandpa, we cannot waste all our resources

272
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:31,055
just trying to find Madrigal.

273
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:33,849
And what do you propose we do?

274
00:15:34,224 --> 00:15:39,647
Ignore the fact that your
traitor of a bodyguard got away?

275
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:43,817
Okay, I understand.
But you said it yourself.

276
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:48,238
He's nothing but an insect
that we'll crush

277
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,324
the minute he decides to come back.

278
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:53,452
For now, we have better things to do.

279
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:58,332
This is a bitter pill to swallow, Arnaldo.

280
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:00,709
[Julio sighs]

281
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:03,712
But, unfortunately, you're right.

282
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:09,760
Emilia…

283
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:12,137
Hi, Aunt Claire.

284
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,683
Care for some wine and a whining session?

285
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,978
What are you whining about,
my dear Emilia?

286
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:25,275
What would you do if your son,
whom you love,

287
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:29,947
suddenly treats you
like garbage for some woman…

288
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,366
Ivy Aguas?

289
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:34,702
What else can you do, Emilia?

290
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,870
You can't sabotage

291
00:16:36,954 --> 00:16:40,290
Ivy and Arnaldo every chance you get.

292
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,669
What are you trying to say, Auntie?

293
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:47,589
Arnaldo may be your son,
but he is his own person.

294
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:50,843
You can't decide whom he should love.

295
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:53,387
The only thing you can do is support him,

296
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:55,723
love him, whatever happens.

297
00:17:01,895 --> 00:17:03,355
Here's your bag, Ivy.

298
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,773
Thanks, Nanny.

299
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:08,444
I'm just waiting for Arnaldo
then we'll go to the co-op.

300
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:11,947
Ivy, isn't it hard for you
that you're with Arnaldo

301
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,616
even though you're
actually supporting Diego?

302
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,537
I need to do this.

303
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:22,207
If I don't, our plans will be ruined.

304
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:25,544
I also need to go
because my mother's there.

305
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:27,880
I need to look out for her
and protect her.

306
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:31,759
-Okay. Just be careful.
-[phone ringing]

307
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:38,599
-Diego.
-Ivy.

308
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:39,516
<i>I'll go there as soon</i>

309
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:42,811
as Arnaldo gets here. Be ready.

310
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:43,896
<i>We will.</i>

311
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,564
Be careful, Ivy.

312
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:47,483
-Of course?
-[Carlotta] Mr. Mayor!

313
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:48,650
<i>Mr. Mayor, you're here.</i>

314
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:51,111
Mr. Mayor is here, Ivy.

315
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:58,869
Mr. Mayor, you're a bit early.

316
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:05,834
Of course.

317
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,545
I'm excited for the grassroots campaign.

318
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:09,671
Who were you talking to?

319
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:13,550
A partner. Business in Manila.

320
00:18:16,011 --> 00:18:19,139
I'm sure today's going to be

321
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:24,103
fruitful and enlightening.

322
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:27,439
Let's go?

323
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:34,613
Mr. Mayor.

324
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:42,246
Diego? Nimfa's co-workers

325
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,956
will be coming all the way
from the other town.

326
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:46,583
But they're all ready to support you.

327
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:49,044
[applause]

328
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:52,047
-Thank you, Mrs. Camia.
-You're welcome, Diego.

329
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,175
-Uncle Pandoy.
-Son.

330
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:57,845
-[Loring] That's right.
-[Pandoy] Thank you, thank you.

331
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:09,314
The Ardientes.

332
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:25,080
Good morning to you all.

333
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,541
Dear friends, how are you all?

334
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:32,671
We're here to give you
some gifts. Please accept them.

335
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:45,142
And what's wrong with you people?

336
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,394
Why won't you accept our gifts?

337
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:52,774
Why? Are you satisfied with
what Camia Cruz is giving you?

338
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:55,194
And what does this woman
have that we don't?

339
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:57,529
Show some decency.

340
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:01,033
You just can't accept that
the people of Ardiente

341
00:20:01,116 --> 00:20:03,493
are rejecting your family's bribes!

342
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:05,787
Who says those are bribes?
They aren't bribes.

343
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,289
They aren't? Why?

344
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:10,250
You're only giving us gifts
so you can force us…

345
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:12,961
-to vote for Mayor Arnaldo!
-You're testing my patience!

346
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:16,924
We came here out of humility.

347
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:21,803
Because I know that
we disagree on a lot of things

348
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,222
here in the cooperative.

349
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,307
And then I arrive here,

350
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:28,477
and I find this Camia woman leading you!

351
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,103
What am I supposed to think?

352
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:34,274
She's poisoned your minds
and those of our neighbors!

353
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,859
[Emilia] Precisely.

354
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:39,655
After all of the help
the Ardientes have given you,

355
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:41,365
this is how you repay us?

356
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:43,242
What are you all so proud of, anyway?

357
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:47,663
Who do you think is capable
of leading this town?

358
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:49,957
Aside from us, the Ardientes?

359
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,126
Who else? Tell us! Who?!

360
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:58,507
[tense music swelling]

361
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:06,056
Me.

362
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:11,270
I will run for governor
against you, Arnaldo.

363
00:21:16,566 --> 00:21:19,653
-Diego for the people!
-Diego for the people!

364
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:23,240
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

365
00:21:23,323 --> 00:21:27,244
-Diego for the people!
-Viva Ardiente!

366
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:29,288
[farmers] Diego for the people!

367
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:31,665
[Ardientes' supporters] Viva Ardiente!

368
00:21:31,748 --> 00:21:33,417
[farmers] Diego for the people!

369
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:36,878
[Julio laughing] You?!

370
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:40,257
Now you're a comedian too.

371
00:21:40,924 --> 00:21:44,136
Who did you take after? Your mother? Hmm?

372
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:49,016
Well, then.

373
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:51,601
Let me ask you this, my fellowmen.

374
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:55,897
Will you really allow
this worthless bastard

375
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:58,066
to become the governor of this town?

376
00:21:58,150 --> 00:21:59,568
No! Mayor Arnaldo!

377
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:03,947
[overlapping dialogue]

378
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:08,201
A good leader isn't measured by his roots…

379
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,495
but by his character.

380
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:16,001
You should never trust a leader
who's a murderer.

381
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:23,800
Yes! Arnaldo had all of
Camia Cruz's witnesses killed.

382
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:27,054
-We'll fight for Diego!
-Viva Ardiente!

383
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:29,181
[farmers] We'll fight for Diego!

384
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:30,849
[Ardientes' supporters] Viva Ardiente!

385
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:34,478
-We'll fight for Diego!
-Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

386
00:22:34,561 --> 00:22:36,480
[overlapping dialogue]

387
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:37,814
[Loring] We'll fight for Diego!

388
00:22:37,898 --> 00:22:39,900
Arnaldo, relax. Not here.

389
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:42,861
There are a lot of people. Relax.

390
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:47,657
Miss Aguas, why are you
trying to stop Arnaldo?

391
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:52,788
He's only giving
what this bastard deserves.

392
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:58,210
Because this worthless man is a traitor!

393
00:22:59,127 --> 00:23:02,798
What now? Cat got your tongue?
That's the truth.

394
00:23:02,881 --> 00:23:06,176
You betrayed our family
with what you're doing.

395
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,261
Think about it, Diego.

396
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:11,348
How dare you compete with your brother?!

397
00:23:11,681 --> 00:23:12,974
Your own flesh and blood!

398
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:15,936
I wouldn't be surprised…

399
00:23:17,104 --> 00:23:19,397
if it was you who helped Madrigal escape.

400
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:22,192
[Julio] You know Madrigal, right?

401
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:25,737
The same Madrigal who killed Governor…

402
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:27,155
-Alvarez!
-Liar!

403
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:30,158
It was you who had Alvarez killed!

404
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:32,369
You're all murderers!

405
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:35,205
You're lower than the dirt on this farm!

406
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:37,165
-That's enough!
-Arnaldo!

407
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:39,918
-Diego!
-Viva Ardiente!

408
00:23:40,001 --> 00:23:42,170
Stop! That's enough! Stop them!

409
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:45,340
[clamoring]

410
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:51,805
[overlapping dialogue]

411
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:56,935
Viva, Ardiente! Viva, Ardiente!
Viva, Ardiente!

412
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:59,020
Viva, Ardiente! Viva, Ardiente!

413
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:00,230
[clamoring]

414
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,273
Diego!

415
00:24:01,356 --> 00:24:03,108
We'll fight for Diego!
We'll fight for Diego!

416
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:05,152
-We'll fight for Diego!
-Viva Ardiente!

417
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:08,029
We'll fight for Diego!
We'll fight for Diego!

418
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:09,364
Viva, Ardiente!

419
00:24:09,447 --> 00:24:13,410
[overlapping dialogue]

420
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:15,662
[clamor continues]

421
00:24:18,748 --> 00:24:19,916
Let's go!

422
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,377
[clamor continues]

423
00:24:25,505 --> 00:24:27,799
[clamoring]

424
00:24:30,177 --> 00:24:32,929
[indistinct shouting]

425
00:24:40,896 --> 00:24:42,022
[laughing]

426
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:46,359
What a joke.

427
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:50,405
You know what?

428
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:56,203
I feel like I'm in an alternate universe.

429
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:57,913
Can you imagine?

430
00:24:57,996 --> 00:25:03,793
Diego used to be the fat, clumsy, crybaby

431
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:06,546
bastard of this family.

432
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:08,381
Look at him now!

433
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,800
He's actually running for governor!

434
00:25:11,384 --> 00:25:12,886
Mark my words.

435
00:25:12,969 --> 00:25:17,724
If that bastard ever wins,
I'll have my head chopped off.

436
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:24,731
Raul, did I say something funny?!

437
00:25:24,814 --> 00:25:25,649
No, Papa.

438
00:25:25,732 --> 00:25:29,069
I was just thinking of an old saying

439
00:25:29,152 --> 00:25:31,738
that if someone feels
threatened or nervous,

440
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:35,951
they usually mask it by laughter
or letting out their anger.

441
00:25:36,034 --> 00:25:37,244
Just like what you're doing.

442
00:25:37,327 --> 00:25:39,955
What if I shove this cane
down your throat?!

443
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:43,708
Papa, please!
Don't vent your anger on Raul.

444
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:47,545
Actually, he's right.
We should be wary of Diego

445
00:25:47,629 --> 00:25:50,298
because he could win
the votes of the masses.

446
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:53,843
Papa, had you let me run in the elections.

447
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:54,970
A woman politician…

448
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,263
-like me.
-[Julio] Here we go again.

449
00:25:56,346 --> 00:25:58,974
You know, I can get the votes of the poor.

450
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:02,560
Cut it out, Mom. You can't win. Accept it.

451
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:05,480
And we'll keep losing if we
let you run in the elections.

452
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:08,149
Wow, Arnaldo! Are you sure you'll win?

453
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:09,234
-Well, yes, I am!
-Oh.

454
00:26:09,317 --> 00:26:10,860
Just stop it!

455
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:16,116
Look at you. This is so stupid!

456
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:18,451
We are punishing each other

457
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:20,078
because of what happened earlier!

458
00:26:20,161 --> 00:26:24,499
When in fact it's them
who deserve our punishment!

459
00:26:24,582 --> 00:26:28,920
To remind those peasants
just who they're dealing with!

460
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:38,054
[Loring] The Ardientes are the worst!

461
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:40,598
They thought they could intimidate us.

462
00:26:40,682 --> 00:26:41,725
And bribe us.

463
00:26:41,808 --> 00:26:43,935
No matter what they give us,

464
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:49,149
I'll never vote for any Ardiente again!

465
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:50,442
-[Pandoy] That's right!
-[Fernan] Yeah!

466
00:26:50,525 --> 00:26:53,445
And they have the nerve to tell us that

467
00:26:53,528 --> 00:26:56,364
Diego helped their prisoner escape.

468
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:59,659
Are those bastards crazy?

469
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:00,660
Doesn't matter.

470
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:04,331
Everyone in the cooperative should unite.

471
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:05,540
I'm for Diego!

472
00:27:05,623 --> 00:27:06,791
-We're all for Diego!
-For Diego!

473
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:11,046
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

474
00:27:11,129 --> 00:27:13,048
-Diego!
-Diego!

475
00:27:13,131 --> 00:27:16,634
Thank you, Uncle. Thank you, everyone.

476
00:27:18,261 --> 00:27:20,138
[suspenseful music playing]

477
00:27:24,851 --> 00:27:26,019
[phone ringing]

478
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:29,773
Hello, Congressman.

479
00:27:29,856 --> 00:27:32,650
Mario, are you still there?

480
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,944
Yes, sir. What is it, sir?

481
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:36,363
Do you need our help?

482
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:37,489
Yes.

483
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:41,576
I want you to teach
Diego Torillo a lesson.

484
00:27:42,660 --> 00:27:44,454
I want you to beat some sense into him.

485
00:27:45,121 --> 00:27:46,289
Yes, Congressman.

486
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:48,416
Let's go.

487
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:55,965
-[Fernan] Like his grandfather.
-[Pandoy] Right.

488
00:27:56,049 --> 00:27:57,842
[Pandoy] Remember how mad
he got when we ignored it?

489
00:27:57,926 --> 00:27:58,718
[Fernan] I know.

490
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:01,805
-All right. Here. Here. Here.
-You're so silly.

491
00:28:01,888 --> 00:28:03,681
Everyone, look.

492
00:28:03,765 --> 00:28:07,227
Diego Torillo. Come with us.

493
00:28:07,602 --> 00:28:10,897
Wait. Who are you? What do you want?

494
00:28:10,980 --> 00:28:12,857
Congressman Ardiente told us
to pick him up.

495
00:28:15,318 --> 00:28:16,861
They have something to discuss.

496
00:28:17,487 --> 00:28:18,905
[Fernan] Hold on a second.

497
00:28:19,906 --> 00:28:22,992
I don't believe you. Get out of here.

498
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:23,910
I said--

499
00:28:23,993 --> 00:28:25,495
-[Camia] Let go of him!
-[farmers clamoring]

500
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:27,914
Go on! Try it!

501
00:28:27,997 --> 00:28:29,165
-Give us your guns!
-I dare you!

502
00:28:29,249 --> 00:28:31,084
-Take their guns!
-Give us your guns!

503
00:28:31,167 --> 00:28:32,043
[Pandoy] Take their guns!

504
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,878
-Leave!
-Get out of here!

505
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:34,879
-Out!
-What now, huh?!

506
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:36,798
-[Camia] Out!
-Get out of here!

507
00:28:36,881 --> 00:28:38,383
Don't ever come back!

508
00:28:38,466 --> 00:28:40,427
-[farmer 1] Don't ever come back here!
-[farmer 2] Get out of here!

509
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:41,845
[Fernan] Tell that to your boss!

510
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:44,139
-Chickens!
-Leave!

511
00:28:45,473 --> 00:28:46,683
[Fernan] Still acting tough?

512
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:05,827
Did you really think you could
get away from me

513
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:07,620
after what you did earlier?

514
00:29:12,041 --> 00:29:15,170
Maybe you forgot I know where you live.

515
00:29:17,881 --> 00:29:18,965
About that…

516
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:21,509
Well, I was quite busy.

517
00:29:22,594 --> 00:29:26,806
But actually, Mr. Mayor,
I was just about to call you

518
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:30,226
because I'm about
to open a bottle of wine.

519
00:29:45,325 --> 00:29:47,118
Let's celebrate, Mr. Mayor.

520
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:49,037
One question, one straight answer.

521
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:51,664
Are you supporting another
candidate in the elections?

522
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:56,169
Where is this coming from, Mister--

523
00:29:56,252 --> 00:29:59,464
I saw you earlier. You helped Diego.

524
00:30:02,801 --> 00:30:03,802
Ow.

525
00:30:07,222 --> 00:30:09,933
May I just remind you, Mr. Mayor…

526
00:30:10,683 --> 00:30:15,939
First, we aren't together
for you to feel jealous.

527
00:30:16,648 --> 00:30:20,401
Second. This day was exhausting.

528
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:23,905
I think I deserve a warm bath.

529
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:28,785
Once you're ready to talk
in a calm manner,

530
00:30:28,868 --> 00:30:31,246
I'm sure you know where to find me.

531
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:49,639
[sensual music playing]

532
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:10,159
[ominous music playing]

533
00:31:30,722 --> 00:31:33,850
[tense music playing]

534
00:31:57,957 --> 00:31:59,667
What are you doing there?

535
00:32:05,256 --> 00:32:06,341
Mr. Mayor.

536
00:32:12,138 --> 00:32:13,681
Why are you here?

537
00:32:18,227 --> 00:32:19,228
Well…

538
00:32:20,855 --> 00:32:22,106
I thought you invited me.

539
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:23,858
Really?

540
00:32:24,651 --> 00:32:26,861
I don't remember inviting you here.

541
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:31,032
I guess you misunderstood
what I said earlier.

542
00:32:31,866 --> 00:32:33,409
Let me explain it to you.

543
00:32:34,327 --> 00:32:36,162
What I meant was…

544
00:32:36,829 --> 00:32:42,502
go home first, and once you're
calm enough to talk to me,

545
00:32:42,877 --> 00:32:46,255
come back here to my house so we can talk.

546
00:32:46,339 --> 00:32:49,425
I didn't say you could
come to my bathroom.

547
00:32:57,016 --> 00:32:58,017
Well…

548
00:33:01,604 --> 00:33:04,232
it's a good thing
I didn't come here to talk.

549
00:33:04,774 --> 00:33:05,775
[suspenseful sting]

550
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:14,867
[groans]

551
00:33:17,912 --> 00:33:18,913
[sighs]

552
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:20,832
[exhales]

553
00:33:22,875 --> 00:33:26,295
Ivy, I told you that the more you do that,

554
00:33:28,423 --> 00:33:30,008
the more I want you.

555
00:33:32,427 --> 00:33:35,471
So, please. Do it again.

556
00:33:36,139 --> 00:33:37,265
Go ahead. Slap me.

557
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:38,808
-Mr. Mayor, please leave.
-No more?

558
00:33:38,891 --> 00:33:40,101
-No more?
-I said leave.

559
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:42,270
No, because I will keep
coming back for more.

560
00:33:42,353 --> 00:33:43,604
Get out.

561
00:33:44,105 --> 00:33:46,315
No more? Is that all?

562
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:48,651
Oh, yes!

563
00:33:48,735 --> 00:33:52,280
-Out of my room!
-Yes! Now, it's my turn.

564
00:33:52,363 --> 00:33:53,364
[Ivy groans]

565
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:56,242
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

566
00:33:57,326 --> 00:33:59,120
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

567
00:34:02,206 --> 00:34:03,207
Arnaldo!

568
00:34:04,917 --> 00:34:07,336
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

569
00:34:08,546 --> 00:34:09,464
[Ivy groans]

570
00:34:09,547 --> 00:34:12,717
[tense music playing]

571
00:34:17,597 --> 00:34:18,598
[Arnaldo grunts]

572
00:34:18,681 --> 00:34:21,184
[groaning]

573
00:34:22,351 --> 00:34:23,311
Ah!

574
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:28,316
You want more? Was that enough?

575
00:34:29,317 --> 00:34:30,860
You want more?

576
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:32,862
Tell me. Do you want more?!

577
00:34:33,654 --> 00:34:37,033
That was below the belt, but I'll take it.

578
00:34:37,617 --> 00:34:38,951
[Arnaldo panting]

579
00:34:39,535 --> 00:34:41,662
What do you want? Huh?

580
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:44,207
What do you really want, Ivy?

581
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:47,168
Look, Arnaldo.

582
00:34:48,544 --> 00:34:52,340
Arnaldo, we don't have to be like this.

583
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:57,261
I'm not easy to get,
like your other women.

584
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:59,263
I'm sorry if I did that to you.

585
00:35:00,056 --> 00:35:01,641
You're just so aggressive.

586
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:07,313
What I want is…

587
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:12,151
I want to know you better first.

588
00:35:12,652 --> 00:35:15,822
I want to know who you
really are, your personality,

589
00:35:15,905 --> 00:35:17,115
and who you are inside.

590
00:35:21,536 --> 00:35:26,332
All you have to do is just make me happy.

591
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:30,837
Then, I'm all yours.
I'll give you everything!

592
00:35:30,920 --> 00:35:32,130
I'm all yours.

593
00:35:33,881 --> 00:35:35,174
Make you happy?

594
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:38,594
Wait.

595
00:35:39,762 --> 00:35:40,763
Ouch.

596
00:35:41,597 --> 00:35:44,684
I thought I wasn't like your other women.

597
00:35:46,727 --> 00:35:47,728
So…

598
00:35:49,313 --> 00:35:50,982
I'm just like them?

599
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:53,776
You just want me to be a bed filler?

600
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:57,572
Arnaldo…

601
00:35:57,655 --> 00:35:58,656
That's not…

602
00:35:58,739 --> 00:36:00,908
-what I'm trying to say.
-No, no, no, no.

603
00:36:00,992 --> 00:36:02,660
Well, if that's what you think of me…

604
00:36:03,744 --> 00:36:05,454
Arnaldo, you can't fool me.

605
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:08,249
You hear that?

606
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:11,502
If you want me to be your girlfriend,

607
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:16,257
if you really want me, you'll respect me.

608
00:36:16,924 --> 00:36:21,012
You won't treat me like your former women.

609
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:27,435
Please go home.

610
00:36:27,518 --> 00:36:28,519
Ivy.

611
00:36:29,979 --> 00:36:30,980
Ivy!

612
00:36:32,523 --> 00:36:35,902
Diego is really testing my patience.

613
00:36:38,738 --> 00:36:43,159
And you three worthless
bastards. You maggots.

614
00:36:43,242 --> 00:36:45,453
Get out of my sight! Leave!

615
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:49,123
You're all idiots!

616
00:36:50,082 --> 00:36:56,088
Papa, this proves that Diego
isn't afraid of us anymore.

617
00:36:56,797 --> 00:37:00,468
And will definitely influence
people to support him.

618
00:37:00,551 --> 00:37:02,345
What do you want me to do, then?

619
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:06,599
Have Diego killed? Or better…

620
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:08,517
Raul is the better choice.

621
00:37:08,601 --> 00:37:12,438
Do you want to keep him as a hostage
so Diego stops going against us?

622
00:37:12,521 --> 00:37:13,439
Is that what you want?

623
00:37:13,522 --> 00:37:15,566
[quietly] This old bastard.

624
00:37:15,650 --> 00:37:16,943
No, Papa.

625
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:20,738
All I'm saying is
we have to do something about it,

626
00:37:20,821 --> 00:37:24,367
or else we'll lose supporters.

627
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:27,036
That is one thing that will never happen

628
00:37:27,119 --> 00:37:31,999
because the one who will defeat
the Ardientes hasn't been born.

629
00:37:32,875 --> 00:37:34,377
It can happen, Papa.

630
00:37:34,877 --> 00:37:38,798
Especially if Arnaldo
continues to be careless.

631
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:40,967
You know your grandson.

632
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:43,844
Instead of pleasing the dirty masses,

633
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:47,974
all he does is flirt with Ivy Aguas.

634
00:37:49,558 --> 00:37:51,143
Stop it, Emilia.

635
00:37:52,645 --> 00:37:54,897
Arnaldo knows what he's doing.

636
00:37:54,981 --> 00:37:58,150
He is going to bring Ivy home.

637
00:37:58,901 --> 00:38:01,862
And if necessary, I'll help him do it.

638
00:38:02,530 --> 00:38:06,075
Now, please. Stop discrediting your son.

639
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:09,662
Whatever you say
won't change my mind, anyway.

640
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:14,333
Arnaldo will be my successor, not you.

641
00:38:15,334 --> 00:38:19,714
Now, you. You're my daughter.
And I love you very much.

642
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:24,427
But… we'll talk about you some other time.

643
00:38:26,554 --> 00:38:27,555
[sighs]

644
00:38:32,059 --> 00:38:32,810
-Arnaldo…
-Ivy.

645
00:38:32,893 --> 00:38:36,355
Arnaldo, please! Please go home.

646
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:40,151
Look, we're hurting each other.

647
00:38:40,651 --> 00:38:42,153
I don't want this.

648
00:38:42,236 --> 00:38:45,281
And I don't understand
what has gotten into you.

649
00:38:45,948 --> 00:38:47,575
Please, just go home.

650
00:38:50,036 --> 00:38:53,289
Fine. I'll admit, I was out of line.

651
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:56,083
I don't want us to fight, either.

652
00:38:56,876 --> 00:39:01,339
It's just that today, I feel
like you're toying with me.

653
00:39:02,256 --> 00:39:03,507
-No.
-Yes!

654
00:39:03,591 --> 00:39:05,676
-How?
-With… with Diego.

655
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:07,053
I don't like it!

656
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:10,973
-You're mine, Ivy.
-[sighs]

657
00:39:11,057 --> 00:39:12,767
-That Diego…
-You're all mine.

658
00:39:12,850 --> 00:39:17,188
Diego… You mean that guy?

659
00:39:18,397 --> 00:39:22,151
Come on, Arnaldo! Can't you see?

660
00:39:22,735 --> 00:39:25,946
I'm just using Diego…

661
00:39:27,531 --> 00:39:31,911
to know what his plans
are against you and your family.

662
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:35,664
You're too possessive, Mr. Mayor.

663
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:40,544
Arnaldo is the jealous type.

664
00:39:41,545 --> 00:39:42,838
And I don't like that.

665
00:39:43,756 --> 00:39:45,341
I hate those kinds of men.

666
00:39:47,468 --> 00:39:48,761
Arnaldo…

667
00:39:51,305 --> 00:39:52,431
Arnaldo…

668
00:39:57,103 --> 00:39:58,354
I'm yours.

669
00:39:59,313 --> 00:40:04,026
I mean, my loyalty is all yours.

670
00:40:05,986 --> 00:40:08,322
Believe me, I'm loyal to you.

671
00:40:12,952 --> 00:40:13,828
Come here.

672
00:40:13,911 --> 00:40:18,124
[upbeat music playing]

673
00:40:21,836 --> 00:40:25,756
You know, just focus on me.

674
00:40:26,841 --> 00:40:30,511
In the end, you'll get what you want.

675
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:44,733
Arnaldo. Arnaldo…

676
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:48,863
You are playing a dangerous game.

677
00:40:56,537 --> 00:40:57,788
[line ringing]

678
00:40:57,872 --> 00:41:02,251
Hello. Ready the car.
We're going somewhere.

679
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:04,712
[ominous music playing]

680
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:21,187
[Carlotta clears throat]

681
00:41:23,105 --> 00:41:24,064
Nanny.

682
00:41:24,148 --> 00:41:25,357
Ivy.

683
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:29,320
Arnaldo here decided to pay a visit.

684
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:32,323
Nanny Carlotta must be
feeling uncomfortable.

685
00:41:33,032 --> 00:41:34,033
Um…

686
00:41:34,450 --> 00:41:39,163
Nanny, can you please escort
Arnaldo to the living room?

687
00:41:39,997 --> 00:41:42,041
I just need to get dressed.

688
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:43,125
[Carlotta] Okay, Ivy.

689
00:41:48,130 --> 00:41:51,550
Well, can I at least have a drink first?

690
00:41:52,134 --> 00:41:54,470
Oh, sure. I'll just get dressed.

691
00:41:54,553 --> 00:41:55,888
I'll be right with you.

692
00:41:57,014 --> 00:41:58,474
Nanny, please keep him company.

693
00:41:58,849 --> 00:41:59,934
Mr. Mayor.

694
00:42:07,316 --> 00:42:08,317
Disgusting.

695
00:42:20,329 --> 00:42:22,248
<i>I feel like you're toying with me.</i>

696
00:42:22,331 --> 00:42:24,375
<i>-How?</i>
<i>-With… with Diego!</i>

697
00:42:24,458 --> 00:42:27,670
<i>That guy? Can't you see?</i>

698
00:42:27,753 --> 00:42:31,465
<i>I'm just using Diego to know</i>

699
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:33,717
<i>what his plans are</i>
<i>against you and your family.</i>

700
00:42:38,472 --> 00:42:41,892
<i>Ivy, I want you to trust me.</i>
<i>Let me protect you</i>

701
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:44,603
<i>because there's nothing</i>
<i>I wouldn't do for you.</i>

702
00:42:44,687 --> 00:42:47,106
<i>-I need to save Jepoy!</i>
<i>-I'll save him.</i>

703
00:42:47,189 --> 00:42:49,024
<i>I'm his friend, so I'll be</i>
<i>the one to save Jepoy.</i>

704
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:50,818
<i>Yes, he's your friend, but I love you!</i>

705
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:53,237
<i>If you get caught, you're done for.</i>

706
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:56,115
<i>I'll die first before that happens.</i>

707
00:43:10,671 --> 00:43:13,674
[phone ringing]

708
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:17,261
[phone ringing]

709
00:43:18,137 --> 00:43:20,055
-Hello, Ivy?
-Diego?

710
00:43:20,139 --> 00:43:22,391
Is there a problem? Why'd you call?

711
00:43:22,474 --> 00:43:24,810
It's about what happened earlier.

712
00:43:24,893 --> 00:43:26,353
<i>I just want to ask how you're doing.</i>

713
00:43:27,187 --> 00:43:28,981
How are the people from the cooperative?

714
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:31,900
How are you? Are you okay?

715
00:43:33,611 --> 00:43:37,990
Of course. I'm tough as nails.
I'm all right.

716
00:43:39,742 --> 00:43:41,952
Uh, Diego, I was just thinking…

717
00:43:42,828 --> 00:43:43,871
<i>now that the Ardientes know about</i>

718
00:43:43,954 --> 00:43:46,081
your candidacy as governor…

719
00:43:47,249 --> 00:43:49,585
I'm sure that they'll go after you.

720
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:52,880
Diego, it's more dangerous now.

721
00:43:53,714 --> 00:43:57,426
I was thinking of giving you bodyguards.

722
00:43:58,469 --> 00:44:01,305
Ivy, after everything we've been through…

723
00:44:02,014 --> 00:44:04,141
you still think I need bodyguards?

724
00:44:04,767 --> 00:44:05,893
<i>I know you're worried.</i>

725
00:44:06,977 --> 00:44:08,646
Ivy, I have my own bodyguards.

726
00:44:09,104 --> 00:44:10,522
<i>The people from the cooperative.</i>

727
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:15,527
No one can protect me
better than they can.

728
00:44:16,236 --> 00:44:18,822
<i>All of them. The people.</i>

729
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:21,659
They're my bodyguards.

730
00:44:23,744 --> 00:44:25,454
Diego, please be careful.

731
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:30,417
I promise. Take care of yourself too.

732
00:44:30,501 --> 00:44:34,880
[tender music playing]

733
00:44:53,649 --> 00:44:57,486
<i>The people are willing to give</i>
<i>up their lives for me, Ivy.</i>

734
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,949
<i>But who will sacrifice their life for you?</i>

735
00:45:20,884 --> 00:45:23,804
Hey. Where are you going?

736
00:45:25,222 --> 00:45:26,348
I'm going to Ivy's.

737
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:29,101
I'll stand guard outside her house.

738
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:31,437
Like a security guard?

739
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:35,899
If that's what it takes
to make sure she's safe.

740
00:45:38,735 --> 00:45:42,156
If that's the case,
you should bring some coffee.

741
00:45:42,239 --> 00:45:45,451
Come on, Loring. He doesn't need that.

742
00:45:45,534 --> 00:45:48,120
As long as it's Ivy,
he's always wide awake.

743
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:52,458
Uncle, come on. Are you still
cracking that joke?

744
00:45:52,541 --> 00:45:56,003
Well, you're the one who hasn't changed.

745
00:45:57,546 --> 00:46:00,215
-Well, Nanny?
-Just take care out there.

746
00:46:00,299 --> 00:46:01,592
[Pandoy] Yes, stay safe.

747
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:04,094
-I'll take care.
-[Loring] Okay.

748
00:46:12,436 --> 00:46:13,437
Do you have a problem?

749
00:46:14,229 --> 00:46:18,525
Mr. Mayor, I don't like
the fact that you harassed Ivy.

750
00:46:19,151 --> 00:46:22,321
You're older than her,
so please respect her.

751
00:46:25,616 --> 00:46:29,036
You know, at our house,
maids like you get punished.

752
00:46:30,662 --> 00:46:33,707
Forgive me, Mr. Mayor,
but this isn't your house.

753
00:46:33,790 --> 00:46:35,250
Yes, I forgive you now.

754
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:40,631
But for a maid, you're a bit meddlesome.

755
00:46:40,714 --> 00:46:45,719
And for a politician,
you're quite perverted.

756
00:46:47,346 --> 00:46:49,223
Again, I don't care what you think.

757
00:46:49,306 --> 00:46:50,307
But be careful.

758
00:46:52,017 --> 00:46:53,560
That might get you into trouble.

759
00:46:54,353 --> 00:46:56,647
And that might be the reason

760
00:46:56,730 --> 00:46:59,358
why you'll lose in the upcoming elections.

761
00:47:07,115 --> 00:47:08,116
[doorbell rings]

762
00:47:18,669 --> 00:47:19,670
Good evening.

763
00:47:19,753 --> 00:47:20,837
Congressman.

764
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:23,340
Where's Miss Aguas?

765
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:33,809
Mr. Mayor.

766
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:38,605
You forgot your eyeglasses.

767
00:47:42,609 --> 00:47:43,610
Thank you.

768
00:47:44,736 --> 00:47:46,905
She's inside, Congressman.

769
00:47:47,656 --> 00:47:49,449
Well then, I think I should come in.

770
00:47:49,533 --> 00:47:50,617
I should--

771
00:47:57,457 --> 00:48:00,168
Ivy, dear. The congressman's here.

772
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:04,673
Congressman.

773
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:08,135
-Grandpa.
-May I join you?

774
00:48:08,218 --> 00:48:11,680
[tense music playing]

775
00:48:16,560 --> 00:48:17,644
<i>I plan to conduct a survey.</i>

776
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:20,814
<i>The public is losing</i>
<i>their trust in the Ardientes.</i>

777
00:48:20,897 --> 00:48:24,443
<i>I can't lose to Diego.</i>

778
00:48:24,526 --> 00:48:27,529
<i>I won't let that happen!</i>

779
00:48:27,613 --> 00:48:31,074
<i>You know what? You are a two-faced bitch!</i>

780
00:48:31,158 --> 00:48:33,827
<i>Diego, just like before.</i>
<i>Nothing will change.</i>

781
00:48:33,910 --> 00:48:36,330
<i>Lily will always be there for you.</i>

782
00:48:41,251 --> 00:48:42,711
[Arnaldo] <i>Well? Should I</i>
<i>get rid of Diego now?</i>

783
00:48:42,794 --> 00:48:46,632
<i>Can you really kill your own brother?</i>

784
00:48:46,715 --> 00:48:49,593
[theme music playing]
